title: Debt-Brake Budget Cuts
subtitle: Chancellor [+ chancellor +] wants to cut social spending to meet the debt brake.
new-page: true
view-if: month >= 11 and spd_in_government == 0 and chancellor_party == "CDU" and unemployment_rate > 6.5 and welfare >= -2 and emergency_cuts_timer = 0
on-arrival: emergency_cuts_seen = 1; emergency_cuts_timer = 12
tags: event
max-visits: 4

= Debt-Brake Budget Cuts

Tax revenue is down and spending on unemployment benefits is up. To keep next year's budget within the debt brake, Chancellor [+ chancellor +]'s government has proposed deep cuts to the Grundsicherung (the former Bürgergeld), to housing benefit and to the Bundesagentur's training programmes.

[? if spd_toleration : The government depends on our votes. If we reject the budget, [+ chancellor +] will probably call a vote of confidence and lose it, and there will be new elections. The workers are against the cuts, but some say that a stable government is worth the price. ?]

- @nothing_to_do: There is nothing we can do.
- @vote_no
- @vote_yes

@nothing_to_do
view-if: spd_toleration == 0
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; unemployment_rate += 0.3; unemployed_afd += 4; unemployed_linke += 3; unemployed_spd += 2; trust_in_democracy -= 3; budget += 1; inflation -= 0.3; economic_growth -= 0.3;

The cuts pass with the votes of the government parties. The AfD and the Linke both use them to recruit, and so do we.


@vote_no
title: Vote against the budget, ending the toleration agreement.
view-if: spd_toleration
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; spd_toleration = 0; trust_in_democracy -= 3
call: set_next_election_time

We vote the budget down. [+ chancellor +] calls a vote of confidence, loses it, and asks the Federal President to dissolve the Bundestag. The Grundsicherung is safe for now, but at what cost?

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].


@vote_yes
title: Vote for the budget to keep the toleration agreement.
view-if: spd_toleration
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; unemployment_rate += 0.3; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; workers_spd *= 0.9; unemployed_spd *= 0.9; unemployed_afd += 5; unemployed_linke += 5; workers_afd += 5; workers_linke += 5; workers_spd -= 4 if welfare < 0; unemployed_spd -= 5 if welfare < 0; trust_in_democracy -= 3; linke_relation -= 8; budget += 1; inflation -= 0.3; economic_growth -= 0.3;

We tell our voters that a stable government is better than another snap election, and that we have softened the worst of the cuts. Few believe us. The AfD and the Linke are delighted.
